            <ArticleTitle>Ruthenium catalyzed remote C4-selective C-H functionalisation of carbazoles via σ-activation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13039-13042</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc07606a</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the C4-selective C-H alkylation of carbazole derivatives furnished with a pyrimidine directing group at N9. This was realized using ruthenium catalyzed σ-activation methodology, whereby C-H activation at C1 enables the interaction of this ruthenacycle, at the para position to the metal center, with tertiary alkyl radicals.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
